= Evidence and Epistemics =
This page defines how BITwiki records evidence quality, epistemic status, confidence, and review processes for claims.
== Epistemic Status Vocabulary ==
Use the following controlled vocabulary for the epistemic status of a claim:
'' '''Speculative''' — A hypothesis or conjecture with limited or indirect support.
'' '''Preliminary''' — Early evidence exists but is limited, fragile, or unreplicated.
'' '''Supported''' — Evidence aligns with the claim, but key gaps or uncertainty remain.
'' '''Well supported''' — Multiple credible sources or lines of evidence converge.
'' '''Established''' — Broad consensus with strong, repeated evidence.
'' '''Disputed''' — Credible sources materially disagree about the claim.
== Confidence Levels ==
Confidence is a numeric level from 0 to 100:
'' 0–19: Very low confidence (mostly speculative)
'' 20–39: Low confidence (weak or indirect support)
'' 40–59: Moderate confidence (some supporting evidence, notable gaps)
'' 60–79: High confidence (multiple consistent sources)
'' 80–100: Very high confidence (strong, repeated, or consensus support)
== Source Requirements ==
'' '''Minimum''' — at least 1 reliable source
'' '''Preferred''' — 2 or more sources for non-trivial or contested claims
'' '''Required for "Well supported" or "Established"''' — multiple independent sources
'' '''If "Disputed"''' — include sources on both sides
== Claim Subobject Structure ==
Every claim should be recorded as a subobject:
<pre>
{{#subobject:Claim-001
 |Has claim text=The tool reduces average task completion time by 20%.
 |Has epistemic status=Supported
 |Has confidence level=65
 |Has confidence rationale=Two internal studies show ~20% improvement.
 |Has source list=<ref>Study A (2024)</ref>
 |Has review status=Needs review
 |Has last reviewed=2026-02-08
 |Has reviewer=User:Example
}}
</pre>
Required properties:
'' Has claim text
'' Has epistemic status
'' Has confidence level (0-100)
'' Has confidence rationale
'' Has source list
'' Has review status
'' Has last reviewed
'' Has reviewer
